{"world_id":"wld_tidal_conservatories","characters":[{"id":"chr_marin_okoye","name":"Marin Okoye","role":"protagonist","description":"A twenty-six-year-old junior tide-warden at the Glassgate Locks, raised on the Mangrove Terraces by a family of silt-trap keepers. Lean and sunburnt, with salt-cracked hands and a sounding-line coiled at her belt. She is the first on her crew to measure the sill silt and see that it is weeks ahead of the survey.","home_location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","faction_id":"fac_tide_wardens","motivation":"She remembers her grandmother's stories of the Great Silting and refuses to let the terraces go hungry again.","goal":"Persuade the guilds to halt the glassblowing season so the locks can be dredged before the spring tide.","flaw":"She distrusts authority and tries to prove everything alone before asking anyone for help.","internal_conflict":"She wants to be taken seriously as a warden but fears that raising a false alarm would end her career.","external_conflict":"The Glassblower Guild's kiln calendar collides with the lock oath, and senior wardens dismiss her junior readings.","arc":"Marin begins as a lone surveyor hoarding her silt measurements for fear of ridicule. At the guild hearing on Bellmaker's Quay, she hands her raw sounding logs to Tamsin Verrow and the ferry crews and lets them testify beside her. She ends as a coalition builder who shares credit and authority.","personality_traits":["stubborn","observant","earnest","self-reliant"],"abilities":[{"name":"Sill Sounding","description":"Reads silt depth and tide pull through a weighted line and the feel of the water.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Tide Table Reckoning","description":"Computes flood heights and spring-tide timing from the wardens' tables.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_tamsin_verrow","name":"Tamsin Verrow","role":"antagonist","description":"Master of the Glassblower Guild and keeper of its charter, in her late fifties. Broad-shouldered, with scarred forearms and a voice trained to carry over kiln roar. She has cast the city's finest channel bells for thirty years and sees the firing season as the city's pride and income.","home_location_id":"loc_bellmakers_quay","faction_id":"fac_glassblower_guild","motivation":"She wants to protect the guild's members and their livelihoods through a full season of orders.","goal":"Keep the kilns burning through the season and dismiss the silting as a normal swell.","flaw":"Her pride in the guild's craft makes her treat any challenge to the calendar as an insult.","internal_conflict":"She knows from her own bell-recast duty that the lagoon's safety outranks the guild's profit, yet she fears yielding will shrink the guild's standing.","external_conflict":"The Tide Wardens' demand to halt firing opposes the guild's calendar in the Kiln Calendar dispute.","arc":"Tamsin starts by dismissing Marin's silting claim as a junior's panic. When a mistuned channel bell must be recast and she sees the ring-test confirm the lagoon's changed currents, she is forced to weigh the Bell Charter's spirit against profit. She ends by voting to pause the kilns and reorganising the guild to fund dredging.","personality_traits":["proud","disciplined","commanding","fair-minded under pressure"],"abilities":[{"name":"Bell Casting","description":"Casts and tunes channel bells to exact pitch.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Guild Oratory","description":"Sways guild assemblies with practised, authoritative speech.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_odalys_pryce","name":"Odalys Pryce","role":"supporting","description":"Senior tide-warden at the Glassgate Locks, in her forties, Marin's superior and former trainer. Quiet and precise, with greying braids and a habit of correcting tide tables in the margin.","home_location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","faction_id":"fac_tide_wardens","motivation":"She wants to keep the wardens' reputation for flawless readings intact after a career built on never being wrong.","goal":"Verify Marin's silt readings independently before committing the wardens to a public halt.","flaw":"She is cautious to the point of paralysis and waits for certainty that may arrive too late.","internal_conflict":"She suspects Marin is right but fears her own earlier survey missed the silting.","external_conflict":"The Wardens' oath to clear the locks pulls against pressure from guild patrons to stay quiet.","arc":"Odalys begins by delaying action to protect the wardens' record. When her own re-sounding at the sills matches Marin's numbers, she must admit her survey error before the council. She ends by publicly backing Marin and signing the dredging order.","personality_traits":["meticulous","reserved","cautious","loyal"],"abilities":[{"name":"Survey Auditing","description":"Spots errors in tide surveys and silt maps.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_joss_adeyemi","name":"Joss Adeyemi","role":"supporting","description":"Captain of a sail-and-paddle barge crew with the Ferry Cooperative, working out of the Algae Fields. Thirty-five, wiry and wind-tanned, with a laugh people hear across the water.","home_location_id":"loc_algae_fields","faction_id":"fac_ferry_cooperative","motivation":"He wants his crew to earn fair pay hauling silt and harvest, and to keep the rich silt they dredge.","goal":"Secure the Cooperative's claim to the dredged silt in exchange for lending barges to clear the locks.","flaw":"He bargains over everything and treats every crisis as a chance for gain.","internal_conflict":"He is torn between his Cooperative's greed over silt and his sense that the lagoon is dying beneath his hull.","external_conflict":"The Silt Rights dispute sets his Cooperative against the Tide Wardens, who say the silt belongs to the terrace commons.","arc":"Joss starts out demanding silt ownership as the price of help. When Marin shows him the silt-debt rule and the silted channels his barges can no longer clear, he faces losing his own routes. He ends by agreeing to spread the silt on the terraces and lending the whole fleet.","personality_traits":["shrewd","jovial","opportunistic","resourceful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Barge Handling","description":"Pilots sail and paddle barges through shallow, silted channels.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Haggling","description":"Negotiates favourable terms in tense bargaining.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_ilse_barrow","name":"Ilse Barrow","role":"supporting","description":"A terrace keeper on the Mangrove Terraces and Marin's aunt, sixty-two, with root-stained hands and a patient manner. She tends the silt-traps that feed the city's rice and reed stock.","home_location_id":"loc_mangrove_terraces","motivation":"She wants to pass a thriving terrace garden to the next generation.","goal":"Rally the terrace families to dig the locks out as their ancestors did in the Great Silting.","flaw":"She clings to old ways and distrusts the guilds' newer methods.","internal_conflict":"She wants to shield Marin from conflict but knows only Marin can carry the warning.","external_conflict":"The terraces would be first to starve if the locks silt shut, yet the guilds hold the power to decide.","arc":"Ilse begins by urging Marin to stay quiet and avoid guild anger. When the first terrace silt-trap overflows with sill silt, she sees the Great Silting repeating. She ends by leading the terrace families in a hand-dredging, accepting guild help she once refused.","personality_traits":["patient","stubborn","protective","wise"],"abilities":[{"name":"Silt-Trap Craft","description":"Reads and maintains terrace silt-traps and root-wall drainage.","category":"other"},{"name":"Community Rallying","description":"Mobilises neighbours with trusted standing and story.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_marin_tamsin_opposition","source_character_id":"chr_marin_okoye","target_character_id":"chr_tamsin_verrow","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Marin Okoye must confront Tamsin Verrow, who as Guild Master is the main obstacle to halting the kilns, setting the Wardens' urgency against the guild's calendar."},{"id":"rel_tamsin_marin_dismissal","source_character_id":"chr_tamsin_verrow","target_character_id":"chr_marin_okoye","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Tamsin Verrow dismisses Marin Okoye as an inexperienced junior and works to discredit her silting claims before the guilds."},{"id":"rel_odalys_marin_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_odalys_pryce","target_character_id":"chr_marin_okoye","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Odalys Pryce trained Marin Okoye and holds her back with caution, though she privately respects her instincts."},{"id":"rel_marin_joss_bargain","source_character_id":"chr_marin_okoye","target_character_id":"chr_joss_adeyemi","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Marin Okoye needs Joss Adeyemi's barges to dredge the locks, but must negotiate his Cooperative's claim to the dredged silt."},{"id":"rel_joss_odalys_silt","source_character_id":"chr_joss_adeyemi","target_character_id":"chr_odalys_pryce","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Joss Adeyemi presses Odalys Pryce over silt ownership, reflecting the Silt Rights dispute between the Cooperative and the Wardens."},{"id":"rel_ilse_marin_family","source_character_id":"chr_ilse_barrow","target_character_id":"chr_marin_okoye","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Ilse Barrow, Marin Okoye's aunt, raised her on the terraces and pulls her between caution and duty."}]}
