uild Master is the main obstacle to halting the kilns, setting the Wardens' urgency against the guild's calendar."},{"id":"rel_tamsin_marin_dismissal","source_character_id":"chr_tamsin_verrow","target_character_id":"chr_marin_okoye","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Tamsin Verrow dismisses Marin Okoye as an inexperienced junior and works to discredit her silting claims before the guilds."},{"id":"rel_odalys_marin_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_odalys_pryce","target_character_id":"chr_marin_okoye","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Odalys Pryce trained Marin Okoye and holds her back with caution, though she privately respects her instincts."},{"id":"rel_marin_joss_bargain","source_character_id":"chr_marin_okoye","target_character_id":"chr_joss_adeyemi","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Marin Okoye needs Joss Adeyemi's barges to dredge the locks, but must negotiate his Cooperative's claim to the dredged silt."},{"id":"rel_joss_odalys_silt","source_character_id":"chr_joss_adeyemi","target_character_id":"chr_odalys_pryce","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Joss Adeyemi presses Odalys Pryce over silt ownership, reflecting the Silt Rights dispute between the Cooperative and the Wardens."},{"id":"rel_ilse_marin_family","source_character_id":"chr_ilse_barrow","target_character_id":"chr_marin_okoye","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Ilse Barrow, Marin Okoye's aunt, raised her on the terraces and pulls her between caution and duty."}]}
