l and has never once been accused of favoring a side. Her ledger is always at her hip.","motivation":"To keep the covenant intact and the record of challenges honest.","goal":"Decide whether the tally-stick binds the sects and see the ruling stand without dividing her own sect.","flaw":"Rigid devotion to precedent that blinds her to what a rule is for.","internal_conflict":"She privately thinks the covenant should bend for peace but fears one exception will unravel it.","external_conflict":"Crane Sect elders and Eel School delegates both press her for a ruling that favors them.","arc":"She starts as a clerk bound to precedent, certain the stick of a disowned student has no standing. After Mei Lin asks her to witness the stick as Hallow's word, she weighs the broken challenge's lesson and rules it binding. She ends as a witness willing to read the covenant by its purpose.","personality_traits":["precise","impartial","reserved","weary"],"abilities":[{"name":"Covenant Law","description":"Knows every precedent of the dueling covenant and can cite it on the spot.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Witness Authority","description":"Her testimony settles disputes at Bannerhall and is accepted by all sects.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_dun_harrow","name":"Dun Harrow","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_saltmarket_isle","faction_id":"fac_salt_wardens","description":"A stout, one-eyed Salt Warden captain in his forties, with a salt-stiffened coat and a brass whistle on a cord. He has guarded envoys on Saltmarket Isle since the aftermath of the Broken Challenge and takes safe conduct as a personal oath.","motivation":"To make sure no envoy is ever harmed on Saltmarket Isle again.","goal":"Keep the moot's envoys safe and the market peace unbroken while the sects argue.","flaw":"Suspicious of everyone, including those who mean to help.","internal_conflict":"He is sworn to neutrality but wants the moot to succeed.","external_conflict":"Hot-headed sect delegates keep testing the market peace with insults and veiled threats.","arc":"He begins by distrusting Mei Lin as a disowned student who could provoke an ambush. After she turns down a covert duel offered on the docks, he extends full safe conduct to her. He ends as an open guarantor of the moot, trading wary neutrality for active protection.","personality_traits":["gruff","watchful","dutiful","dry-humored"],"abilities":[{"name":"Safe Conduct Authority","description":"His whistle summons wardens and his word grants envoys safe passage.","category":"social"},{"name":"Dockside Combat","description":"Uses a boarding pike and brawler's footwork to subdue disputes without drawing blades.","category":"physical"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_hallow_mei_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_oren_hallow","target_character_id":"chr_mei_lin_ashwren","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Master Oren Hallow took in Mei Lin Ashwren after her disowning and trained her in Thunder Reed Dojo, then bound her to his tally-stick mission without full disclosure, which strains her trust in his memory."},{"id":"rel_mei_kesh_rival","source_character_id":"chr_mei_lin_ashwren","target_character_id":"chr_kesh_tidebrand","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Mei Lin Ashwren and Kesh Tidebrand clash over whether the tally-stick binds the Eel School, and he intends to void it by defeating her in a formal challenge."},{"id":"rel_kesh_mei_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_kesh_tidebrand","target_character_id":"chr_mei_lin_ashwren","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Kesh Tidebrand sees Mei Lin Ashwren as the carrier of an obligation that threatens his school's claim to the rookery shallows, and he presses her publicly at every meeting."},{"id":"rel_sora_mei_judge","source_character_id":"chr_sora_vael","target_character_id":"chr_mei_lin_ashwren","relationship_type":"judge","description":"Sora Vael must rule on whether Mei Lin Ashwren's tally-stick still binds the sects, and her precedent-bound doubts about a disowned carrier create the central obstacle at Bannerhall."},{"id":"rel_dun_mei_guardian","source_character_id":"chr_dun_harrow","target_character_id":"chr_mei_lin_ashwren","relationship_type":"wary guardian","description":"Dun Harrow distrusts Mei Lin Ashwren as a possible source of trouble on Saltmarket Isle but is sworn to protect her as an envoy, which creates friction until she earns his trust."},{"id":"rel_sora_kesh_adversary","source_character_id":"chr_sora_vael","target_character_id":"chr_kesh_tidebrand","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Sora Vael enforces the covenant against Kesh Tidebrand's attempts to bend the nesting ban, and her rulings on the Rookery Rights keep him bound to her record."}]}
