cal"},{"name":"Ledger Forensics","description":"Spots inconsistencies between mass ledger entries, duty logs and salvage tallies.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Power-Draw Analysis","description":"Reads residual power signatures from hull systems using a handheld spectrometer and tap meter.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_tomas_reyes","name":"Tomas Reyes","role":"supporting","description":"A 55-year-old union steward who keeps the heat rosters in the Mirror Shed. He is broad-shouldered and has a limp from the Austerity-era safety rewrite. He is the gatekeeper for who works sunside and when, and he is respected and slightly feared.","home_location_id":"loc_mirror_shed","faction_id":"fac_riggers_union","motivation":"He wants to keep the safety charter intact so nobody else dies the way his crew did in the Sail Fire.","goal":"Protect the heat roster from Helio Tank's demands for longer shifts and keep the union's leverage in the audit.","flaw":"He bends roster entries quietly when it protects his people, and he refuses to admit that it is a form of the fraud he opposes.","internal_conflict":"He demands honest logs from others while privately fudging his own roster to shield riggers.","external_conflict":"Helio Tank pressures him to extend sunside shifts, while the auditors threaten to examine his rosters.","arc":"He begins as a steward who shields the union by massaging records. When Maren brings him her raw logs and the auditors begin to examine the rosters, he has to choose between hiding his own edits and backing her evidence. He ends by correcting his roster on the record, taking the penalty, and giving the union's backing to an open audit.","personality_traits":["protective","gruff","pragmatic","secretive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Roster Management","description":"Balances crew heat budgets and shift rotations to maximise safe sunside time.","category":"social"},{"name":"Safety Charter Knowledge","description":"Knows every clause of the safety charter and 