cal"},{"name":"Ledger Forensics","description":"Spots inconsistencies between mass ledger entries, duty logs and salvage tallies.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Power-Draw Analysis","description":"Reads residual power signatures from hull systems using a handheld spectrometer and tap meter.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_tomas_reyes","name":"Tomas Reyes","role":"supporting","description":"A 55-year-old union steward who keeps the heat rosters in the Mirror Shed. He is broad-shouldered and has a limp from the Austerity-era safety rewrite. He is the gatekeeper for who works sunside and when, and he is respected and slightly feared.","home_location_id":"loc_mirror_shed","faction_id":"fac_riggers_union","motivation":"He wants to keep the safety charter intact so nobody else dies the way his crew did in the Sail Fire.","goal":"Protect the heat roster from Helio Tank's demands for longer shifts and keep the union's leverage in the audit.","flaw":"He bends roster entries quietly when it protects his people, and he refuses to admit that it is a form of the fraud he opposes.","internal_conflict":"He demands honest logs from others while privately fudging his own roster to shield riggers.","external_conflict":"Helio Tank pressures him to extend sunside shifts, while the auditors threaten to examine his rosters.","arc":"He begins as a steward who shields the union by massaging records. When Maren brings him her raw logs and the auditors begin to examine the rosters, he has to choose between hiding his own edits and backing her evidence. He ends by correcting his roster on the record, taking the penalty, and giving the union's backing to an open audit.","personality_traits":["protective","gruff","pragmatic","secretive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Roster Management","description":"Balances crew heat budgets and shift rotations to maximise safe sunside time.","category":"social"},{"name":"Safety Charter Knowledge","description":"Knows every clause of the safety charter and how to invoke it in disputes.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_ines_valcourt","name":"Ines Valcourt","role":"antagonist","description":"A 47-year-old senior liaison for the Helio Tank Consortium at the Bastion Hulk. She is composed and immaculately dressed in a heat-shielded suit liner, and she speaks softly. She rose by making the yard's numbers balance, whatever that took.","home_location_id":"loc_bastion_hulk","faction_id":"fac_helio_tank","motivation":"She wants the consortium's spare hulls kept off the mass ledger, because declaring them would force write-downs that would end her career and the consortium's margins.","goal":"Keep the hull in Shadow Dock out of the audit and discredit any rigger who reports it.","flaw":"She believes every problem can be managed with paperwork and pressure, so she underestimates people who work from physical evidence.","internal_conflict":"She started her career as an honest accountant and tells herself that hiding spares is protecting jobs, not committing fraud.","external_conflict":"The Charter Audit Office is closing in on the ledger, and the ten-minute light delay slows her ability to get direction from the consortium's inner-system owners.","arc":"She starts as a confident fixer who is sure the paper trail will hold. When Maren's power-draw evidence reaches Auditor Dara Whitlock and contradicts the ledger entries Ines signed, her managed solution collapses. She ends by trying to flee blame by offering a partial confession that implicates the consortium, a choice that confirms she is still trying to manage the numbers instead of owning them.","personality_traits":["poised","calculating","persuasive","self-justifying"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger Manipulation","description":"Reclassifies hull entries and salvage mass to hide spares from review.","category":"social"},{"name":"Institutional Leverage","description":"Uses the consortium's ownership of the yard charter to pressure crews and officials.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_dara_whitlock","name":"Dara Whitlock","role":"supporting","description":"A 42-year-old lead charter auditor assigned to the Bastion Hulk audit berth. She is angular and unhurried, with close-cropped grey hair and a habit of reading documents twice. She has seized ledgers before and is known for being fair to the point of coldness.","home_location_id":"loc_bastion_hulk","faction_id":"fac_charter_audit","motivation":"She wants an audit finding that holds up, because a previous audit she led was overturned for relying on testimony instead of evidence.","goal":"Establish whether hulls are being hidden off the mass ledger, using only evidence that can survive appeal.","flaw":"She is so rigid about procedure that she dismisses credible evidence if it arrives outside the proper channel.","internal_conflict":"She wants to be impartial but suspects that her procedural rigidity has let past fraud slip through.","external_conflict":"Ines Valcourt and the consortium challenge the audit's authority, and the light delay slows any appeal or confirmation.","arc":"She begins as an auditor who refuses anything outside formal procedure. When Maren submits raw power-draw logs verified by Tomas Reyes, she must decide whether to accept evidence that did not come through the audit office. She chooses to accept it with an independent check on Shadow Dock, ending as an auditor who weighs the evidence itself rather than the channel it came through.","personality_traits":["methodical","impartial","reserved","exacting"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger Seizure Authority","description":"Empowered to seize and impound the mass ledger and associated records.","category":"social"},{"name":"Audit Analysis","description":"Cross-references mass, power and duty records to find discrepancies.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_pell_adeyemi","name":"Pell Adeyemi","role":"supporting","description":"A 26-year-old dock hand and Maren's former apprentice, who now works shifts at Shadow Dock. He is wiry and nervous, with a stammer when lying. He took the Shadow Dock posting because it paid extra heat credits and has never asked what is berthed there.","home_location_id":"loc_shadow_dock","faction_id":"fac_riggers_union","motivation":"He wants enough heat credits to leave the yard and bring his sister inward from the outer belt.","goal":"Keep his Shadow Dock posting and the pay that comes with it without learning anything he would have to report.","flaw":"He avoids confronting uncomfortable facts, preferring not to know what he might have to act on.","internal_conflict":"He suspects the hull he maintains is not scrapped, but he is afraid that admitting it would cost him his sister's passage.","external_conflict":"Ines Valcourt's office controls his posting and pay, and Maren's investigation threatens both.","arc":"He starts as a hand who looks away to keep his posting. When Maren asks him to confirm the hull's power draw, and Ines's office hints he will lose his posting, he has to choose. He ends by giving Maren access to Shadow Dock and testifying on record, accepting the loss of his posting to stop avoiding what he knows.","personality_traits":["anxious","loyal","evasive","earnest"],"abilities":[{"name":"Dock Maintenance","description":"Maintains cradles, tethers and power couplings in an eclipsed dry dock.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Thermal Discipline","description":"Works long cold-side shifts with disciplined heat budgeting.","category":"physical"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_maren_pell_mentee","source_character_id":"chr_maren_okafor","target_character_id":"chr_pell_adeyemi","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Maren Okafor trained Pell Adeyemi as a rigger. She trusts him, which makes his silence about Shadow Dock more painful and her need for his help more urgent."},{"id":"rel_pell_maren_debt","source_character_id":"chr_pell_adeyemi","target_character_id":"chr_maren_okafor","relationship_type":"former apprentice","description":"Pell Adeyemi owes Maren Okafor his skills but fears what her investigation will cost him, so he avoids her even as she needs him."},{"id":"rel_maren_tomas_union","source_character_id":"chr_maren_okafor","target_character_id":"chr_tomas_reyes","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Maren Okafor relies on Tomas Reyes for roster access and union backing. Her demand for clean records puts his quiet roster edits at risk."},{"id":"rel_ines_maren_foe","source_character_id":"chr_ines_valcourt","target_character_id":"chr_maren_okafor","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Ines Valcourt sees Maren Okafor as the main threat to hidden spares and uses pressure on rosters and postings to discredit her."},{"id":"rel_ines_pell_leverage","source_character_id":"chr_ines_valcourt","target_character_id":"chr_pell_adeyemi","relationship_type":"manipulator","description":"Ines Valcourt controls Pell Adeyemi's Shadow Dock posting and pay, and she uses that control to keep him quiet about the hull."},{"id":"rel_dara_ines_audit","source_character_id":"chr_dara_whitlock","target_character_id":"chr_ines_valcourt","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Dara Whitlock audits the ledger entries Ines Valcourt signed, and the two clash over the audit office's authority to seize records."},{"id":"rel_tomas_ines_pressure","source_character_id":"chr_tomas_reyes","target_character_id":"chr_ines_valcourt","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Tomas Reyes resists Ines Valcourt's push for longer sunside shifts, and she in turn threatens to expose his roster edits."},{"id":"rel_maren_dara_evidence","source_character_id":"chr_maren_okafor","target_character_id":"chr_dara_whitlock","relationship_type":"uneasy ally","description":"Maren Okafor needs Dara Whitlock to accept her evidence, while Dara Whitlock's insistence on formal procedure threatens to reject it."}]}
