{"world_id":"wld_seedways","characters":[{"id":"chr_maren_voss","name":"Maren Voss","role":"protagonist","description":"A weathered woman in her late forties, Maren is the lead seed-keeper of the caravan. She has walked the seedways since girlhood, her palms scarred by twine and sealing wax, her grey braid tied with a strip of oilcloth. She was trained at Granary Hill and carries the sealed seed stock in a lead-lined chest that never leaves her sight.","home_location_id":"loc_granary_hill","faction_id":"fac_seed_keepers","motivation":"To see the valley towns plant before the last frost so that no one goes hungry through another winter.","goal":"Lead the caravan through Ford Market and the Ash Orchards and over the Frost Gate before it closes, with the seed stock graded and intact.","flaw":"Stubborn pride in the keepers' honor makes her unable to entertain the idea that a keeper could be at fault.","internal_conflict":"She wants to believe the order is blameless, yet she half-remembers seeing her mentor sign off a short measure years ago.","external_conflict":"The Cut Grain dispute: millers blame her order for diluted tithe grain, and the Orchard Families accuse her of diverting their promised stock.","arc":"Maren begins certain that the keepers cannot be at fault and treats every accusation as an insult. At the Ford Market weigh-house she finds chaff-cut grain bearing a keeper's seal, and must choose between burying it to protect the order or exposing it under rul_grain_truth. She chooses to expose it, striking her own mentor's name from the caravan rolls, and ends the story trusting honest accounting over inherited pride.","personality_traits":["resolute","dry-humored","watchful","proud","tender with seedlings"],"abilities":[{"name":"Seed Grading","description":"Can judge viability and purity of grain by touch, smell and a single cracked kernel.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Long-Road Endurance","description":"Decades of caravan travel let her march through bad weather and rough passes with little rest.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Frost Reading","description":"Predicts the last frost from sky, bird movement and the feel of the morning air.","category":"other"}]},{"id":"chr_tobin_ashby","name":"Tobin Ashby","role":"supporting","description":"A lanky nineteen-year-old apprentice keeper with ink-stained fingers and a patched wool coat too short in the sleeves. He joined the caravan from a hill orphanage and keeps a tally-book of every measure carried, copying the grading marks as if they were scripture.","home_location_id":"loc_granary_hill","faction_id":"fac_seed_keepers","motivation":"To earn a keeper's seal and a name that will be carried by the caravans after him.","goal":"Pass his first full circuit without losing a single measure, and be sworn in at the Frost Gate.","flaw":"Eagerness to please makes him hide mistakes rather than report them.","internal_conflict":"He idolizes the order but is beginning to see its elders bend the rules he was taught to revere.","external_conflict":"He notices a discrepancy in the sealed sacks that could implicate his senior keepers, and Maren's suspicion lands on him first.","arc":"Tobin starts as an apprentice who conceals a miscounted sack out of fear. When the weigh-house inspection at Ford Market exposes the discrepancy, he confesses publicly and hands Maren his tally-book as evidence. He ends the story as a sworn keeper whose honesty is the order's proof of repair.","personality_traits":["earnest","anxious","meticulous","quick to blush"],"abilities":[{"name":"Tally-Keeping","description":"Keeps exact running counts of sacks and measures in his head and in his book.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Pack-Beast Handling","description":"Calms and leads the caravan's mules through narrow paths and river fords.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_edda_halloran","name":"Edda Halloran","role":"antagonist","description":"The stout, sharp-eyed head miller of the Millers' Compact, in her sixties, with flour permanently worked into the creases of her knuckles. She keeps the weigh-house ledgers at Ford Market and holds the market charters, and still carries resentment from the Millers' Split that cost her family a generation of trade.","home_location_id":"loc_ford_market","faction_id":"fac_millers_compact","motivation":"To restore the Compact's standing and recover the trade her family lost when the routes split.","goal":"Prove that the keepers are cutting tithe grain, and win the right to weigh all seed before it is sealed.","flaw":"Grudge-driven certainty leads her to accuse without proof and to bend the ledgers to support her case.","internal_conflict":"She knows the old falsified ledger was a Compact hand's work, yet she has built her authority on blaming the keepers.","external_conflict":"She blocks the caravan's passage through Ford Market and demands the keepers surrender their seals to Compact inspection.","arc":"Edda begins by leveraging the Cut Grain dispute to tighten the Compact's grip on the market. When Maren brings the chaff-cut sacks and the old falsified ledger page is laid beside the new one, she must admit the forgery began in her own weigh-house. She ends by opening the ledgers to joint inspection, giving up her sole authority to mend the seedway.","personality_traits":["shrewd","unyielding","fair in small things","bitter"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger Reading","description":"Spots altered figures and mismatched hands in tithe ledgers at a glance.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Market Authority","description":"Her charter word can open or close trading at Ford Market.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_joss_pell","name":"Joss Pell","role":"supporting","description":"A quiet weigh-house clerk of about thirty, thin and stooped, with a habit of rubbing chaff-dust from his sleeves. He works under Edda Halloran at Ford Market and has quietly diluted tithe grain for two seasons to cover a hidden shortfall in the Compact's storehouse.","home_location_id":"loc_ford_market","faction_id":"fac_millers_compact","motivation":"To keep the Compact's failing storehouse from being exposed and protect his sister's family who depend on his wage.","goal":"Keep the shortfall hidden until after the harvest returns, when he plans to repay it.","flaw":"Cowardice: he chooses small concealments over honest admission, and each lie requires another.","internal_conflict":"He knows the diluted seed will starve orchards that trust it, but fear of ruin keeps him silent.","external_conflict":"Tobin's tally and Maren's grading are closing in on the weigh-house, and Edda's accusations threaten to expose him.","arc":"Joss begins by quietly cutting tithe grain and letting the keepers take the blame. When Tobin's tally-book points to the weigh-house and Edda demands answers, he sees the Orchard Families will plant the diluted stock. He confesses to Edda and Maren and works the weigh-house scales to replace the bad measures, ending as an honest clerk bearing the cost of his deception.","personality_traits":["timid","observant","guilt-ridden","precise"],"abilities":[{"name":"Weigh-House Craft","description":"Handles scales and measures so finely that small adulterations go unnoticed.","category":"other"},{"name":"Forgery Hand","description":"Can imitate the marks and handwriting of others on ledgers and seals.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_rowan_thistlewood","name":"Rowan Thistlewood","role":"supporting","description":"A broad-shouldered orchard elder in his fifties with sun-cracked hands and a graft-knife always at his belt. He leads the Orchard Families on the blight-ash rows, where his family took the worst land first and has buried more saplings than they have raised.","home_location_id":"loc_ash_orchards","faction_id":"fac_orchard_families","motivation":"To secure grafting stock for the ash rows so his people's long sacrifice is finally repaid.","goal":"Extract the vault grain and grafting stock promised to the orchards before the Frost Gate closes.","flaw":"Old wounds make him treat every offer as a trick, and he escalates before he listens.","internal_conflict":"He needs the caravan's help to survive but believes accepting it means admitting his families were abandoned.","external_conflict":"The Orchard Claims: he believes the vaults are favoring the caravan and has threatened to turn the caravan back at the orchard boundary.","arc":"Rowan starts by barring the caravan from the orchard rows and demanding payment in full. When Maren shows him the sealed stock marked for the orchards and offers his planters first grading rights, he must decide whether to trust the keepers again. He accepts the grafting stock and shares his own cuttings in return, ending as a partner in the seedway rather than a creditor of it.","personality_traits":["blunt","patient with trees","distrustful","fiercely loyal"],"abilities":[{"name":"Grafting","description":"Joins cuttings to rootstock so they survive on poor ash soil.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Soil Sense","description":"Reads blight-ash ground for what will take and what will not.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_ilse_corwin","name":"Ilse Corwin","role":"supporting","description":"A sharp-tongued former keeper in her seventies who was struck from the rolls years ago and now guides travelers over the Frost Gate. She is wiry, with a knotted scarf and a limp from a winter caught beyond the pass. Her name is no longer carried by the caravans.","home_location_id":"loc_frost_gate","motivation":"To clear her name or at least see the truth of her disgrace spoken aloud before she dies.","goal":"Get Maren to examine the old seals and prove who actually adulterated the stock she was blamed for.","flaw":"Resentment makes her withhold what she knows until she is begged, costing others time they cannot spare.","internal_conflict":"She wants vindication but fears the truth may show her own carelessness allowed the adulteration.","external_conflict":"The closing of the Frost Gate leaves her only a narrow window to deliver her evidence before the caravan crosses and winter seals the pass.","arc":"Ilse begins as a bitter gatekeeper who refuses to speak of her past. When Maren arrives with chaff-cut sacks bearing a keeper's seal, Ilse has to choose between staying silent in her grievance or giving up the old seal-mark that identifies the real culprit. She hands it over and guides the caravan through the gate before it closes, ending reconciled with the choice she made to speak.","personality_traits":["acerbic","resourceful","proud","weather-wise"],"abilities":[{"name":"Pass Guiding","description":"Knows every shelter and safe line over the Frost Gate in all weather.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Seal Lore","description":"Recognizes the marks and wax of each keeper's seal across generations.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_maren_tobin_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","target_character_id":"chr_tobin_ashby","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Maren Voss trains Tobin Ashby as her apprentice, but her pride in the order pressures him to hide his mistakes, which creates the secrecy that endangers them both."},{"id":"rel_maren_edda_rival","source_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","target_character_id":"chr_edda_halloran","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Maren Voss and Edda Halloran each blame the other's order for the Cut Grain, and their mutual accusations block the caravan at Ford Market."},{"id":"rel_edda_joss_employer","source_character_id":"chr_edda_halloran","target_character_id":"chr_joss_pell","relationship_type":"employer","description":"Edda Halloran relies on Joss Pell to keep the weigh-house ledgers, unaware that his concealed adulteration is the source of the accusations she aims at the keepers."},{"id":"rel_joss_tobin_threat","source_character_id":"chr_joss_pell","target_character_id":"chr_tobin_ashby","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Joss Pell lets suspicion fall on Tobin Ashby's sacks to hide his own cutting of tithe grain, putting the apprentice in direct danger of being blamed."},{"id":"rel_rowan_maren_creditor","source_character_id":"chr_rowan_thistlewood","target_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Rowan Thistlewood accuses Maren Voss of carrying the orchards' promised grafting stock to the caravan instead, and threatens to turn her away at the orchard boundary."},{"id":"rel_ilse_maren_former_keeper","source_character_id":"chr_ilse_corwin","target_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Ilse Corwin, a keeper struck from the rolls, holds the seal-lore that can confirm Maren Voss's suspicions about a keeper's hand in the Cut Grain, but she withholds it until Maren earns her trust."},{"id":"rel_edda_rowan_trade","source_character_id":"chr_edda_halloran","target_character_id":"chr_rowan_thistlewood","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Edda Halloran and Rowan Thistlewood share a distrust of the keepers and quietly coordinate claims against the vaults, which amplifies the pressure on Maren Voss's caravan."}]}
