h a ruddy face and chronic ink on his cuffs. He has spent decades in the Counting Halls and has built a comfortable standing there by never being linked to an error.","home_location_id":"loc_counting_halls","faction_id":"fac_scribes_order","motivation":"He wants to protect his decades of unblemished standing and the comfort that comes with it.","goal":"Bury the discovery of the miscast tally before it can be traced to his desk or his section.","flaw":"Self-serving cowardice: he will let a junior take the blame rather than risk his own reputation.","internal_conflict":"He once taught Ilse that every entry is a promise to the dead, and he knows he is now betraying that lesson.","external_conflict":"The scribes are under accusation from the weighers, and he is the senior who would be called to account for his section's errors.","arc":"Pell begins by trying to quash Ilse's report to protect himself. When the audit narrows toward his section and Ilse refuses to take the blame, he is forced to choose between denial and testimony, and he admits the slip was his, in his own hand, saving Ilse and a soul. He ends diminished in rank but restored in honour.","personality_traits":["genial","evasive","vain","nostalgic"],"abilities":[{"name":"Scribe's Seal","description":"As a senior scribe, his seal supplies the scribe's key for corrections.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_ilse_pell_supervisor","source_character_id":"chr_ilse_marrow","target_character_id":"chr_pell_quill","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Pell Quill is Ilse Marrow's supervisor and former teacher. His wish to bury the miscast tally directly threatens her effort to report it."},{"id":"rel_ilse_oswin_ally","source_character_id":"chr_ilse_marrow","target_character_id":"chr_oswin_tallow","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Ilse Marrow turns to Oswin Tallow for the weigher's key and warrant. Their uneasy partnership crosses the scribe-weigher blame divide."},{"id":"rel_corvane_ilse_antagonist","source_character_id":"chr_corvane_ashgrave","target_character_id":"chr_ilse_marrow","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Warden Corvane Ashgrave bars Ilse Marrow from the sealed ledgers and treats her correction as a threat to the archive."},{"id":"rel_corvane_oswin_rival","source_character_id":"chr_corvane_ashgrave","target_character_id":"chr_oswin_tallow","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Warden Corvane Ashgrave and Oswin Tallow are on opposite sides of the access dispute, since Corvane demands a weigher's warrant that Oswin has been unwilling to give."},{"id":"rel_pell_oswin_blame","source_character_id":"chr_pell_quill","target_character_id":"chr_oswin_tallow","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Pell Quill blames the weighers, including Oswin Tallow, for the miscast tallies, which feeds the scribes-versus-weighers dispute."}]}
