 judge debts fairly, because the senior tallykeepers still treat her as a copyist.","goal":"Settle the Favour Shortage by ruling which debts ride with the fair.","flaw":"She follows written rules too literally and freezes when the rules do not cover a case.","internal_conflict":"She wants to be seen as fair, but fears that a wrong ruling will cost her the apprenticeship.","external_conflict":"More favours are owed than can be kept before closing day, and the senior tallykeepers are watching her rulings.","arc":"Starts as a nervous copyist who only reads the tags as written. When she finds the misfiled Ninth Stall tag and must choose between the old filing and Marrowyn's claim, she makes her first independent ruling to read the tag by its intent. She ends as a confident judge who weighs the spirit of a debt as well as the letter.","personality_traits":["earnest","meticulous","anxious","curious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Tag Memory","description":"Recalls where every wishing tag hangs in the barn.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Fair Hearing","description":"Listens to both sides of a dispute without interrupting.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_hester_bloom","name":"Hester Bloom","role":"supporting","description":"The silver-haired head of the Stallholders' Round, a rival tea merchant with a stall of copper urns and a tall hat decorated with brass bells. She is brisk and elegant, and she remembers every favour owed to her.","home_location_id":"loc_kettle_commons","faction_id":"fac_stallholders","motivation":"To keep the Round's votes steady, since she fears a reopened Ninth Stall will upend the balance of the stalls.","goal":"Persuade the Round to vote against reviving the Ninth Stall's old lease.","flaw":"She is vain about her standing and cannot bear to be outdone in her own trade.","internal_conflict":"She admires Marrowyn's blends but cannot admit it without feeling that she has lost status.","external_conflict":"The Favour Shortage forces the Round to choose which stalls ride with the fair, and Marrowyn's claim threatens her allies' seats.","arc":"Starts as Marrowyn's polished rival who works to block the claim. After losing a blind tasting contest to Marrowyn at the Kettle Commons, she must choose between her vanity and the Round's vote. She ends by casting the deciding vote in Marrowyn's favour and trading a favour for a place beside the Ninth Stall.","personality_traits":["elegant","competitive","shrewd","proud"],"abilities":[{"name":"Vote Counting","description":"Predicts how each stallholder will vote.","category":"social"},{"name":"Fine Palate","description":"Distinguishes blends and origins from a single sip.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_marrowyn_oswin_claim","source_character_id":"chr_marrowyn_tansy","target_character_id":"chr_oswin_carter","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Marrowyn Tansy and Oswin Carter are rivals over the Ninth Stall's lease: she holds the family claim while he is secretly selling it, and each blocks the other's goal."},{"id":"rel_marrowyn_hester_rivalry","source_character_id":"chr_marrowyn_tansy","target_character_id":"chr_hester_bloom","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Marrowyn Tansy and Hester Bloom are trade rivals in the Kettle Commons, and Hester's influence over the Round's vote can decide Marrowyn's claim."},{"id":"rel_pell_marrowyn_ally","source_character_id":"chr_pell_wick","target_character_id":"chr_marrowyn_tansy","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Pell Wick helps Marrowyn Tansy by finding the misfiled Ninth Stall tag, and in turn Marrowyn gives Pell's first independent ruling a real case to decide."},{"id":"rel_oswin_pell_scrutiny","source_character_id":"chr_oswin_carter","target_character_id":"chr_pell_wick","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Oswin Carter fears that Pell Wick's careful tag-reading will expose his hidden lease sale, so he tries to keep the Tallykeepers' attention elsewhere."},{"id":"rel_hester_oswin_ally","source_character_id":"chr_hester_bloom","target_character_id":"chr_oswin_carter","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Hester Bloom quietly backs Oswin Carter's sale of the lease, since keeping the Ninth Stall closed protects her allies' seats in the Round."}]}
</Output>
