{"reason": "'avast ye' is a common pirate term", "pass": false, "score": 0.0}"},{"role":"user","content":"<Output>
{"world_id":"wld_thistledown","characters":[{"id":"chr_marrowyn_tansy","name":"Marrowyn Tansy","role":"protagonist","description":"A weathered hedge-witch in her early forties who blends teas from roadside herbs and sells them from a handcart. She is small and sun-browned, with moss-green mittens, a patched plum coat and a ring of dried chamomile pinned to her hat. Her family held the Ninth Stall until a promised favour went unkept past the third bell a generation ago, and she has followed the fair every leap-season since.","home_location_id":"loc_kettle_commons","faction_id":"fac_stallholders","motivation":"To restore her family's name and finally brew at the stall her grandmother once kept.","goal":"Claim the Ninth Stall's lease before the third bell of closing day.","flaw":"She hoards her own favours and will not ask anyone for help, so every debt she carries stays private.","internal_conflict":"She believes the forfeit was her family's shame, yet suspects the fair's rules were bent against them.","external_conflict":"The Carter Kin are quietly selling the lease, and she owes more favours than she can keep before the fair moves.","arc":"Starts as a proud, solitary merchant who trusts no one with her debts. At the Wishing Barn she finds her grandmother's unkept favour tag and must publicly ask the Kettle Commons merchants to help keep it before closing day. Having accepted help, she ends the story claiming the lease as part of a community rather than a lone claimant.","personality_traits":["stubborn","warm","observant","proud","dryly funny"],"abilities":[{"name":"Hedge Blending","description":"Brews teas that calm tempers and loosen tongues.","category":"supernatural"},{"name":"Herb Lore","description":"Knows field and hedge plants and their uses by sight and smell.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Haggling","description":"Strikes careful bargains that leave both sides content.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_oswin_carter","name":"Oswin Carter","role":"antagonist","description":"A broad, soft-spoken elder of the Carter Kin who drives the lead wain and keeps the lanes' secrets. He wears a coat of stitched wool patches, one for every field the fair has visited, and carries a brass lane-key on a cord. He has quietly arranged to sell the Ninth Stall's lease to a wealthy buyer.","home_location_id":"loc_leap_lane","faction_id":"fac_carters","motivation":"To fund new wains and repairs, because the Carter Kin's old wheels are failing and the fair cannot move without them.","goal":"Complete the sale of the Ninth Stall's lease before closing day.","flaw":"He keeps secrets out of habit and lets half-truths stand where one plain word would do.","internal_conflict":"He values the fair's promises above all, yet he is bending the lease rule that protects the forfeiting family.","external_conflict":"Marrowyn's claim could void his sale, and the Tallykeepers may scrutinise how he hid the lease from her.","arc":"Starts as a quiet seller who hides the lease sale behind lane-secrets. When Marrowyn challenges him to a tea-tasting contest at the Kettle Commons, he loses and must confess the sale to the Tallykeepers. He ends by bargaining a shared lease that also pays for the wain repairs, no longer hiding behind secrets.","personality_traits":["patient","secretive","practical","courteous"],"abilities":[{"name":"Lane Knowing","description":"Can sense where the lanes will fold and where they will open.","category":"supernatural"},{"name":"Wain Craft","description":"Repairs and drives the great fair wains.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_pell_wick","name":"Pell Wick","role":"supporting","description":"A young apprentice tallykeeper with ink-stained cuffs and an oversized ledger. She is round-faced and freckled, with a quill behind each ear. She tends the wishing tags in the barn and has recently noticed that one old tag was filed out of order.","home_location_id":"loc_wishing_barn","faction_id":"fac_tallykeepers","motivation":"To prove she can judge debts fairly, because the senior tallykeepers still treat her as a copyist.","goal":"Settle the Favour Shortage by ruling which debts ride with the fair.","flaw":"She follows written rules too literally and freezes when the rules do not cover a case.","internal_conflict":"She wants to be seen as fair, but fears that a wrong ruling will cost her the apprenticeship.","external_conflict":"More favours are owed than can be kept before closing day, and the senior tallykeepers are watching her rulings.","arc":"Starts as a nervous copyist who only reads the tags as written. When she finds the misfiled Ninth Stall tag and must choose between the old filing and Marrowyn's claim, she makes her first independent ruling to read the tag by its intent. She ends as a confident judge who weighs the spirit of a debt as well as the letter.","personality_traits":["earnest","meticulous","anxious","curious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Tag Memory","description":"Recalls where every wishing tag hangs in the barn.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Fair Hearing","description":"Listens to both sides of a dispute without interrupting.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_hester_bloom","name":"Hester Bloom","role":"supporting","description":"The silver-haired head of the Stallholders' Round, a rival tea merchant with a stall of copper urns and a tall hat decorated with brass bells. She is brisk and elegant, and she remembers every favour owed to her.","home_location_id":"loc_kettle_commons","faction_id":"fac_stallholders","motivation":"To keep the Round's votes steady, since she fears a reopened Ninth Stall will upend the balance of the stalls.","goal":"Persuade the Round to vote against reviving the Ninth Stall's old lease.","flaw":"She is vain about her standing and cannot bear to be outdone in her own trade.","internal_conflict":"She admires Marrowyn's blends but cannot admit it without feeling that she has lost status.","external_conflict":"The Favour Shortage forces the Round to choose which stalls ride with the fair, and Marrowyn's claim threatens her allies' seats.","arc":"Starts as Marrowyn's polished rival who works to block the claim. After losing a blind tasting contest to Marrowyn at the Kettle Commons, she must choose between her vanity and the Round's vote. She ends by casting the deciding vote in Marrowyn's favour and trading a favour for a place beside the Ninth Stall.","personality_traits":["elegant","competitive","shrewd","proud"],"abilities":[{"name":"Vote Counting","description":"Predicts how each stallholder will vote.","category":"social"},{"name":"Fine Palate","description":"Distinguishes blends and origins from a single sip.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_marrowyn_oswin_claim","source_character_id":"chr_marrowyn_tansy","target_character_id":"chr_oswin_carter","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Marrowyn Tansy and Oswin Carter are rivals over the Ninth Stall's lease: she holds the family claim while he is secretly selling it, and each blocks the other's goal."},{"id":"rel_marrowyn_hester_rivalry","source_character_id":"chr_marrowyn_tansy","target_character_id":"chr_hester_bloom","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Marrowyn Tansy and Hester Bloom are trade rivals in the Kettle Commons, and Hester's influence over the Round's vote can decide Marrowyn's claim."},{"id":"rel_pell_marrowyn_ally","source_character_id":"chr_pell_wick","target_character_id":"chr_marrowyn_tansy","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Pell Wick helps Marrowyn Tansy by finding the misfiled Ninth Stall tag, and in turn Marrowyn gives Pell's first independent ruling a real case to decide."},{"id":"rel_oswin_pell_scrutiny","source_character_id":"chr_oswin_carter","target_character_id":"chr_pell_wick","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Oswin Carter fears that Pell Wick's careful tag-reading will expose his hidden lease sale, so he tries to keep the Tallykeepers' attention elsewhere."},{"id":"rel_hester_oswin_ally","source_character_id":"chr_hester_bloom","target_character_id":"chr_oswin_carter","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Hester Bloom quietly backs Oswin Carter's sale of the lease, since keeping the Ninth Stall closed protects her allies' seats in the Round."}]}
</Output>
