's slow spin.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Arbiter's Cadence","description":"Her formal manner calms heated disputes and draws out contradictions in testimony.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_corvin_shale","name":"Corvin Shale","role":"antagonist","description":"A broad-shouldered free pilot with a salt-white braid and a cracked sail-glove, Corvin Shale flies a patched ketch called the Tallow Gull. He is the pilot holding the stolen perihelion chart. A veteran of the Pilots' Compact, he lost his brother to a sealed route that was charted wrongly, and he calls his possession of the map salvage.","home_location_id":"loc_tether_docks","faction_id":"fac_free_pilots","motivation":"To keep a perihelion route no guild can withhold, so no more pilots die on charts they were forbidden to question.","goal":"Hold onto the chart through the burn and fly the fleet's pilots out on his own route.","flaw":"Grief makes him certain he is right and deaf to evidence that the map's route may be dangerous in other hands.","internal_conflict":"He knows the theft endangers the Compact's hard-won arbitration rights, but cannot give up the only thing that proves his brother's death was avoidable.","external_conflict":"The guild wants him branded a pirate, and the ice barons are buying the tethers he needs to leave before the burn.","arc":"Starts as a defiant pilot hoarding the chart as proof and weapon. When Brannock Ostrel's tether grab strands his own crew over unpaid ice-tithes, he has to choose between keeping the map or trading it to survive. He ends by laying the chart open before the Long Hall, giving up sole possession to save the fleet.","personality_traits":["defiant","charismatic","grief-stricken","fiercely loyal","reckless"],"abilities":[{"name":"Plume Piloting","description":"Threads ketches through crowded tethers using short reaction plume bursts.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Route Memory","description":"Remembers hazards and currents of every route he has flown.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Crew Rallying","description":"Inspires pilots to follow him through desperate manoeuvres.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_brannock_ostrel","name":"Brannock Ostrel","role":"antagonist","description":"An ice baron with rings on every finger and a coat lined with frost-fox fur, Brannock Ostrel presides over the richest claims in the Core Vaults. He speaks softly and pays his debts in full, which he considers proof of his honour. He is buying tethers ahead of the burn.","home_location_id":"loc_core_vaults","faction_id":"fac_ice_barons","motivation":"To secure the baronial claims against the scattering of the fleet and keep his family's holdings the wealthiest in the next orbit.","goal":"Corner enough tethers before perihelion to control which ships leave and on what terms, and obtain the perihelion chart for himself.","flaw":"Avarice cloaked as prudence; he cannot imagine a deal that does not leave him ahead.","internal_conflict":"He prides himself on lawful dealing but is edging toward bribing arbiters and breaching the burn articles.","external_conflict":"The free pilots resist his tether grab, and Isolde's investigation threatens to expose his dealings in the stolen chart's resale.","arc":"Starts as a courteous monopolist convinced his tether purchases are legal prudence. When Isolde presents evidence in the Long Hall that he bought the resold chart, the burn articles force him to settle or forfeit all claims. He ends diminished, releasing the tethers to keep his claims.","personality_traits":["soft-spoken","calculating","patient","vain","scrupulous in appearance"],"abilities":[{"name":"Claim Law","description":"Expert at using the burn articles and ice-tithe rules to pressure debtors.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Tether Brokerage","description":"Manages networks of agents buying berth and tether rights quietly.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_wren_tamsin","name":"Wren Tamsin","role":"supporting",{"id":"PLACEHOLDER"}}],"relationsh