's slow spin.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Arbiter's Cadence","description":"Her formal manner calms heated disputes and draws out contradictions in testimony.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_corvin_shale","name":"Corvin Shale","role":"antagonist","description":"A broad-shouldered free pilot with a salt-white braid and a cracked sail-glove, Corvin Shale flies a patched ketch called the Tallow Gull. He is the pilot holding the stolen perihelion chart. A veteran of the Pilots' Compact, he lost his brother to a sealed route that was charted wrongly, and he calls his possession of the map salvage.","home_location_id":"loc_tether_docks","faction_id":"fac_free_pilots","motivation":"To keep a perihelion route no guild can withhold, so no more pilots die on charts they were forbidden to question.","goal":"Hold onto the chart through the burn and fly the fleet's pilots out on his own route.","flaw":"Grief makes him certain he is right and deaf to evidence that the map's route may be dangerous in other hands.","internal_conflict":"He knows the theft endangers the Compact's hard-won arbitration rights, but cannot give up the only thing that proves his brother's death was avoidable.","external_conflict":"The guild wants him branded a pirate, and the ice barons are buying the tethers he needs to leave before the burn.","arc":"Starts as a defiant pilot hoarding the chart as proof and weapon. When Brannock Ostrel's tether grab strands his own crew over unpaid ice-tithes, he has to choose between keeping the map or trading it to survive. He ends by laying the chart open before the Long Hall, giving up sole possession to save the fleet.","personality_traits":["defiant","charismatic","grief-stricken","fiercely loyal","reckless"],"abilities":[{"name":"Plume Piloting","description":"Threads ketches through crowded tethers using short reaction plume bursts.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Route Memory","description":"Remembers hazards and currents of every route he has flown.","