rty monsoons and lost a brother to the Year of Three Envoys' sort of deadlock.","home_location_id":"loc_envoy_house","faction_id":"fac_majlis","motivation":"To get the fleet away on the first true wind so no captain's crew starves in port.","goal":"Persuade the court to rule quickly, even if it means one envoy yields.","flaw":"His impatience makes him push for speed over fairness.","internal_conflict":"He values the Majlis's unity but is tempted to sacrifice the weakest captains to secure a slot.","external_conflict":"The envoys' rival claims stall the court while the Majlis's slots are held hostage.","arc":"Ishaq starts by demanding speed at any cost and threatening to sail without the court's leave. After Anjali shows him that sailing early would break the wind law and forfeit the whole fleet's standing, he chooses to hold the Majlis together and wait for the pilots. He ends as a patient negotiator who accepts a compromise slot order.","personality_traits":["blunt","loyal","impatient","experienced"],"abilities":[{"name":"Fleet Bargaining","description":"Speaks for dozens of captains and can swing their collective weight in negotiation.","category":"social"},{"name":"Sea Reading","description":"Can read weather and swell almost as well as a pilot.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_leela_pillai","name":"Leela Pillai","role":"supporting","description":"A sharp-eyed pepper factor in her forties, dressed in saffron silk and heavy gold bangles, who inherited a bonded warehouse row from her late husband. She trades in whispers and gifts.","home_location_id":"loc_pepper_warehouses","faction_id":"fac_pepper_factors","motivation":"To get her stored pepper onto the first ships and protect her warehouse from ruin.","goal":"Smooth the first slot toward the envoy who carries her cargo, without being tied to the gifts.","flaw":"She treats generosity as a tool and cannot trust any favour she did not buy.","internal_conflict":"She is ashamed of the gifts she gave but fears honesty will cost her the season.","external_conflict":"The unregistered gifts in her warehouses threaten to implicate her in the scandal around the slot-keepers.","arc":"Leela begins by quietly feeding gifts to the slot-keepers and denying them. When Anjali offers her a chance to enter the gifts in the register before the court names her, she risks her season by confessing and swearing over pepper. She ends as the witness who breaks Rustam's hold, trading her secrecy for her standing.","personality_traits":["shrewd","charming","guarded","generous"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cargo Accounting","description":"Knows every bale, weight and owner in the bonded rows.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Gift Diplomacy","description":"Uses well-timed gifts to open doors across the port.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tomas_vidal","name":"Tomas Vidal","role":"supporting","description":"The master pilot of the Pilot Ghat, a lean man in his sixties with a weathered face and white linen. Bound by the Ghat Oath, he reads the sea each dawn from the harbour steps and alone declares the monsoon turned.","home_location_id":"loc_pilot_ghat","motivation":"To keep the ghat's declaration honest and uncorrupted, as the oath requires.","goal":"Declare the turn at the true moment, whatever pressure the envoys and court apply.","flaw":"His rigid pride makes him refuse to share his reading even when it would help.","internal_conflict":"He fears his aging eyes may misread the sea, yet dares not admit it publicly.","external_conflict":"Envoys and factors press him to hasten or delay the declaration to suit their claims.","arc":"Tomas starts by withholding his readings from everyone, including the court. When the envoys' deadlock and a veiled bribe test the Ghat Oath, he chooses to confide his uncertainty to Anjali and share the signs openly. He ends as a pilot who declares the turn publicly with the court's witness, protecting both the oath and his pride.","personality_traits":["austere","incorruptible","proud","watchful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Monsoon Reading","description":"Interprets swell, cloud and bird flight to judge the turn of the wind.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_anjali_rustam_conflict","source_character_id":"chr_anjali_menon","target_character_id":"chr_rustam_khoury","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Anjali Menon, a scribe sworn to the ledger, investigates Rustam Khoury, the senior slot-keeper whose unregistered gifts and altered filings threaten her ruling."},{"id":"rel_rustam_leela_patron","source_character_id":"chr_rustam_khoury","target_character_id":"chr_leela_pillai","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Rustam Khoury takes gifts from Leela Pillai, who in return expects favoured treatment for her cargo, binding both to the gift scandal."},{"id":"rel_ishaq_anjali_pressure","source_character_id":"chr_ishaq_barakat","target_character_id":"chr_anjali_menon","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Ishaq Barakat presses scribe Anjali Menon to rule fast on the first slot, pressure that tempts her to cut procedural corners."},{"id":"rel_tomas_anjali_trust","source_character_id":"chr_tomas_vidal","target_character_id":"chr_anjali_menon","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Tomas Vidal comes to confide his readings of the sea to Anjali Menon, giving her the timing she needs to settle the slot before the wind turns."},{"id":"rel_leela_anjali_witness","source_character_id":"chr_leela_pillai","target_character_id":"chr_anjali_menon","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Leela Pillai ends up testifying to Anjali Menon about the unregistered gifts, giving her the evidence against Rustam Khoury."}]}
