{"world_id":"wld_lantern_parish","characters":[{"id":"chr_wren_aldous","name":"Wren Aldous","role":"protagonist","description":"A lean, soot-fingered woman of twenty-six, newly sworn as the parish lamplighter after the previous keeper's sudden departure. She came from a lowland market town where she trimmed street lamps, and she carries a cracked horn lantern she refuses to replace. She has a habit of counting things twice and wears her dead mother's wool shawl pinned with a brass wick-pick.","home_location_id":"loc_keepers_croft","faction_id":"fac_lamp_wardens","motivation":"She needs this post to earn the right to stay in a place where no one knows what she left behind in the lowlands.","goal":"Learn which night the cut ledger page recorded and keep the wall lit every night until she knows.","flaw":"She hides unwelcome facts from others to keep her footing, and she trusts her own tally over anyone's word.","internal_conflict":"She wants to belong to the parish yet suspects belonging means joining its silence about the missing night.","external_conflict":"The wardens and the council both stonewall her about the Missing Page while the wall burns short of oil.","arc":"Wren begins as a secretive newcomer who keeps private tallies and tells no one what she finds. When she discovers the croft's wick bench records a night the wall nearly went dark, she must choose between burying it to protect her post or reading it aloud at the Moot Kirk. She chooses to speak, ending as a keeper who trusts the parish with hard truths.","personality_traits":["watchful","stubborn","methodical","guarded","dry-humoured"],"abilities":[{"name":"Wick Cutting","description":"She trims and sets wicks so they burn slow and steady through a full night.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Tally Memory","description":"She can recall the lit and unlit state of every lantern on the wall after a single walk.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_osric_vane","name":"Osric Vane","role":"antagonist","description":"The aging clerk of the Moot Council, broad-shouldered and stooped, with ink-stained cuffs and a voice worn soft from decades of reading nights aloud. He has kept the ledger at the Moot Kirk for thirty winters and speaks of it as if it were scripture.","home_location_id":"loc_moot_kirk","faction_id":"fac_moot_council","motivation":"He believes the parish survives only on the certainty of its record and will protect that certainty at any cost.","goal":"Keep the cut page's night from ever being spoken, so the ledger stays whole in the parish's mind.","flaw":"He treats the written record as more real than the people it serves.","internal_conflict":"He knows the ledger now holds a lie, yet he cannot bear to admit the book he guards is broken.","external_conflict":"The wardens demand to see the ledger, and Wren's questions threaten to expose what he concealed.","arc":"Osric starts as a rigid keeper of an unblemished record, certain that silence protects the parish. When Wren lays the wick bench tally before the council and it contradicts his ledger, he must either burn the evidence or amend the book. He amends the ledger, ending as a clerk who lets the truth stand even though it breaks the page.","personality_traits":["precise","dignified","evasive","fearful","pious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger Authority","description":"His word on what was entered carries the weight of law in council.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_hester_marl","name":"Hester Marl","role":"supporting","description":"Senior Lamp Warden, a gaunt woman in her sixties with a milky left eye and hands scarred by decades of hot oil. She trained the previous lamplighter and now trains Wren, rationing her words as carefully as she rations oil.","home_location_id":"loc_lantern_wall","faction_id":"fac_lamp_wardens","motivation":"She wants to protect the guild's name and the apprentices who might be blamed if the wall truly went dark.","goal":"Make sure Wren keeps the wall lit while the guild is cleared of the Missing Night.","flaw":"She is loyal to the guild above justice and answers questions with orders.","internal_conflict":"She suspects her guild's silence caused the loss she fears being blamed for, and cannot decide whether to confess.","external_conflict":"The council blames the wardens for the cut page while the turf-cutters accuse her of over-counting the oil call-in.","arc":"Hester starts as a closed-mouthed enforcer of guild loyalty who deflects every question. When the turf-cutters' shortfall shows the wall truly burning low, she must choose between defending her over-count and admitting it. She admits the count was wrong in open council, ending as a warden who values honesty over the guild's pride.","personality_traits":["taciturn","stern","loyal","tired"],"abilities":[{"name":"Oil Reckoning","description":"She estimates the oil a night will burn by the smell and colour of the flame.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Wall Lore","description":"She knows every niche, lamp and flaw on the boundary wall.","category":"other"}]},{"id":"chr_tamsin_creel","name":"Tamsin Creel","role":"supporting","description":"A freckled turf-cutter in her thirties with peat-dark forearms, who speaks for the bog families at the oil call-in. She knows the Bog Hollow paths by sound and has lost a brother to its wrong-carrying voices.","home_location_id":"loc_bog_hollow","faction_id":"fac_turf_cutters","motivation":"She wants her family's hearth spared from a tithe she believes is inflated, and her brother's loss explained.","goal":"Force a fair recount of the oil owed so the turf-cutters are not ruined at midwinter.","flaw":"She holds grudges and assumes anyone from the wall is cheating her.","internal_conflict":"She fears the wall's light is the only thing keeping the bog from taking more of her kin, yet resents paying for it.","external_conflict":"The wardens' oil call-in threatens her family's hearth, and the bog line forbids her from carrying a lantern past dusk.","arc":"Tamsin begins as a bitter accuser who distrusts everyone at the wall. When Wren walks the bog edge with her at dusk and shows the true oil count, Tamsin must decide whether to trust a warden's tally. She pays a share of the oil willingly and ends as an ally who stands with the wall.","personality_traits":["fierce","proud","suspicious","loyal to kin"],"abilities":[{"name":"Bog Sense","description":"She finds safe footing in the Bog Hollow by sound and smell, even without light.","category":"physical"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_wren_osric_ledger","source_character_id":"chr_wren_aldous","target_character_id":"chr_osric_vane","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Wren Aldous presses Osric Vane for the cut ledger page, while Osric stonewalls her to protect the record, which sets the lamplighter against the clerk."},{"id":"rel_osric_hester_blame","source_character_id":"chr_osric_vane","target_character_id":"chr_hester_marl","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Osric Vane blames Hester Marl and the wardens for the silence around the Missing Night, and Hester blames his ledger in return, sharpening the council and guild conflict."},{"id":"rel_hester_wren_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_hester_marl","target_character_id":"chr_wren_aldous","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Hester Marl trains Wren Aldous in the craft of the wall but withholds the guild's secrets, so her teaching both guides and restrains Wren."},{"id":"rel_tamsin_hester_oil","source_character_id":"chr_tamsin_creel","target_character_id":"chr_hester_marl","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Tamsin Creel accuses Hester Marl of over-counting the oil call-in, and Hester refuses to concede, which feeds the Oil Shortfall dispute."},{"id":"rel_wren_tamsin_trust","source_character_id":"chr_wren_aldous","target_character_id":"chr_tamsin_creel","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Wren Aldous and Tamsin Creel are wary at first, but Wren's honest count of the oil gradually earns Tamsin's trust and draws them together against the silence."}]}
